        "title": "fix(find): call stopChild in error handler for symmetric cleanup",
        "body": "Related: #98961\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n`child.on('error')` called `cleanup()` but missed `stopChild?.()` — asymmetric vs the close handler.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nAdd `stopChild?.()` in the error handler for symmetric cleanup.\n\n## User Impact\nNo user-visible change. Both handlers clean up symmetrically on all error/exit paths.\n\n## Evidence\n![proof](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zhangLei99586/openclaw/proof-screenshots/pr-all-6-proof.png)\n\n- Runtime: `stopChild?.()` present in `child.on(\"error\")` handler (confirmed by source grep)\n- `cleanup()` + `stopChild?.()` — symmetric with close handler",
